  "notes": "A gospel-quartet-trained piano producer bridging hip-hop soul and gospel, 1995–2010; the band is \"70–100 straight\", marked `[LOW-CONF]`, used as written with the mode at 88. Three drum deltas from \"hip-hop kit under gospel harmony — kick on 1 with a pickup, snare/clap flat on 2&4, 16th hats; on the gospel records a live-feel kit with tambourine on the backbeat\": the kick's secondary anchor sits on `1a` (the pickup), the snare is a clap stack pushed 2–7 ms with `quantizeStrength` at 0.64, and the percussion is a downbeat-placed tambourine/conga/shaker bed at three to six hits a bar with `tambourineMirrorsClap` true — that last is the live-feel gospel layer stated in the entry. The identifying parameter is harmonic and it comes from his training: he \"began as a **session pianist**… and is a member of the traditional-quartet group The Soul Seekers; expect functional major/minor with passing chords and modulation, not modal vamps\". So every family is a functional turnaround, a `vii°` passing family is authored, `susOrDimProb` is raised and `maxChords` is 6 — the opposite of this lane's two-chord default. \"Quartet-style four-part backgrounds\" is the counter at −12 with `octave_echo` sharing top weight, and the melody carries a gospel arch with a real leap share. The bass \"follow[s] the gospel bass line (root-to-third-to-fifth walk-ups) rather than a static sub\", so `followRootsProb` is 0.5 with ascending triad cells and no `bass808` block. ⚠ Confidence is **low**, and the research says why: \"background, instrument and credits sourced; the parametric detail is gospel-genre inference and marked\". The drum and bass claims both carry `[LOW-CONF]` marks, repeated here. ⚠ Every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"gospel harmonic language — he began as a **session pianist** (DJ Quik's *Safe + Sound*, 1995) and is a member of the traditional-quartet group The Soul Seekers\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
